1
00:00:03,879 --> 00:00:06,799
Do you see me as a woman?

2
00:00:06,882 --> 00:00:08,884
Do you actually like me?

3
00:00:08,968 --> 00:00:10,678
Or not really?

4
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:13,431
That's what I came to find out.

5
00:00:18,394 --> 00:00:20,479
Because I was married to my "X"

6
00:00:20,563 --> 00:00:24,150
I had my child at 26,
so my kid is 21 and in college now.

7
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:26,152
Looking back, it was emotional abuse.

8
00:00:30,322 --> 00:00:31,866
I want to feel that spark again.

9
00:00:31,949 --> 00:00:34,452
I want to fall for you more each day.

10
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:37,580
Is dating as a single mom really hard?

11
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:42,334
I came here to find my last love.

12
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:45,921
Wow.

13
00:00:55,181 --> 00:00:56,891
That's what I'm asking you to tell me!

14
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:59,727
I just think, "Come on, don't be lame."

15
00:01:01,687 --> 00:01:03,981
That was really hard for me.

16
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,941
I could barely sleep.

17
00:01:06,025 --> 00:01:07,234
I won't.

18
00:01:07,318 --> 00:01:09,403
I'd never do that.

19
00:01:09,487 --> 00:01:12,823
I never want to go through that again.

20
00:01:26,003 --> 00:01:26,837
What?

21
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:32,134
If I could,

22
00:01:32,218 --> 00:01:36,472
I'd like to start over
from the beginning with you.

23
00:01:36,555 --> 00:01:38,766
-Exactly!
-Exactly!

24
00:01:45,064 --> 00:01:48,400
Love Transit 35+ starts now!

25
00:01:48,484 --> 00:01:49,860
Yes!

26
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,862
Wow, it's finally starting.

27
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:54,114
Speaking of Love Transit 35+…

28
00:01:54,198 --> 00:01:55,741
"This show features 10 men and women

29
00:01:55,825 --> 00:01:58,452
living in a hotel,
distanced from their daily lives,

30
00:01:58,536 --> 00:02:01,497
enjoying a hotel vacation
or hocance as they search for love.

31
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:04,124
And we are here to watch over them,

32
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:05,709
in the mature version of Love Transit."

33
00:02:05,793 --> 00:02:06,627
Mature version.

34
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:09,421
That's right. "To enter Love Transit,

35
00:02:09,505 --> 00:02:11,882
participants must join
alongside their former partners,

36
00:02:11,966 --> 00:02:14,093
otherwise known as their "X."

37
00:02:14,176 --> 00:02:15,719
That's the core condition of Love Transit.

38
00:02:15,803 --> 00:02:17,096
This time,

39
00:02:17,179 --> 00:02:19,932
there is also an age restriction

40
00:02:20,015 --> 00:02:21,642
requiring all men and women
to be 35 or over."

41
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:23,602
-A bit more mature, isn't it?
-A bit more mature.

42
00:02:23,686 --> 00:02:24,728
That's right.

43
00:02:24,812 --> 00:02:26,480
"On the final day, members will choose

44
00:02:26,564 --> 00:02:29,358
their future romantic partners
and confess their feelings.

45
00:02:29,441 --> 00:02:31,443
Will that be someone new

46
00:02:31,527 --> 00:02:32,862
they meet on this hocance?

47
00:02:32,945 --> 00:02:35,656
Or will they get back together
with their X?

48
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:38,325
This show documents the troubles
and tribulations of these adults

49
00:02:38,409 --> 00:02:41,328
as they navigate through love."

50
00:02:41,412 --> 00:02:43,247
By the way,
have you ever watched Love Transit?

51
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:44,665
Of course, I've watched every season.

52
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:46,041
You have?

53
00:02:46,125 --> 00:02:47,710
Wow.

54
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:09,565
Mao-san is very pretty.

55
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:12,735
She doesn't look over 35.

56
00:03:12,818 --> 00:03:14,403
She's very pretty.

57
00:03:16,322 --> 00:03:17,698
He looks uncomfortable.

58
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:21,201
Are you nervous? You don't seem nervous.

59
00:03:22,745 --> 00:03:25,456
Kaede-san, she's also pretty.

60
00:03:25,539 --> 00:03:26,665
They're all pretty.

61
00:03:28,918 --> 00:03:31,670
She looks so mature.

62
00:03:34,798 --> 00:03:36,550
He's very sleek.

63
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:41,138
Misato-san.

64
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,181
Cute.

65
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:43,265
She's pretty as well.

66
00:03:46,518 --> 00:03:48,103
He's giving bad-boy vibes.

67
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:51,357
Kanako-san.

68
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:53,150
That's a lot of blinking!

69
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:54,485
That's some blinking.

70
00:03:56,153 --> 00:03:57,488
Hikaru-san.

71
00:03:57,571 --> 00:03:59,698
He looks unique.

72
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:03,577
So refined.

73
00:04:03,661 --> 00:04:05,412
Now, that's a man over 35.

74
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:16,173
"Please have someone

75
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:18,634
open the letter from the vase on the table

76
00:04:18,717 --> 00:04:21,470
and read it to the group."

77
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:22,596
It's so red.

78
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,764
This?

79
00:04:23,847 --> 00:04:25,933
-I was wondering what that was.
-This must be it.

80
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:31,021
"The flowers in this vase

81
00:04:31,105 --> 00:04:32,648
represent the participants' history

82
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:35,401
through their colors and quantities."

83
00:04:35,859 --> 00:04:37,152
History?

84
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:40,781
"White flowers represent

85
00:04:41,532 --> 00:04:42,783
people who have never married.

86
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:46,120
Blue flowers represent

87
00:04:46,203 --> 00:04:48,330
people who have been married before."

88
00:04:48,414 --> 00:04:51,208
-I see.
-Is that what they mean?

89
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,793
So it's five white and five blue.

90
00:04:52,876 --> 00:04:54,044
It's five and five.

91
00:04:54,128 --> 00:04:55,713
So half and half.

92
00:04:56,505 --> 00:04:57,965
It's five and five?

93
00:04:58,048 --> 00:04:59,550
It's five and five.

94
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:00,759
I was surprised.

95
00:05:01,427 --> 00:05:02,928
At that point,

96
00:05:03,012 --> 00:05:04,513
I started to wonder who could it be?

97
00:05:04,596 --> 00:05:06,557
Is it that person, or this person?
You know?

98
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,684
The numbers don't match.

99
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:11,854
When I stopped to think about it,
why was it five?

100
00:05:11,937 --> 00:05:14,982
Does it mean they were married to someone
other than their X?

101
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:19,028
"Now then, enjoy a meaningful hocance

102
00:05:19,111 --> 00:05:21,864
and may you and your X

103
00:05:21,947 --> 00:05:23,824
find your next wonderful romance."

104
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:27,953
FIVE PEOPLE WHO HAVE NEVER MARRIED,
FIVE PEOPLE WHO HAVE BEEN MARRIED

105
00:05:28,037 --> 00:05:30,330
So they married someone who's not their X.

106
00:05:30,414 --> 00:05:31,874
So that's what that means.

107
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:33,292
It has to be, if it's five and five.

108
00:05:59,026 --> 00:06:01,695
Look at that amazing camera work.

109
00:06:05,574 --> 00:06:06,700
They're switching already.

110
00:06:06,784 --> 00:06:07,701
What is this?

111
00:06:07,785 --> 00:06:09,953
This is one of the show's
signature filming moves.

112
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:20,005
Everyone's smiling.

113
00:06:20,089 --> 00:06:21,799
You're right.

114
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:23,092
Long time no see!

115
00:06:23,175 --> 00:06:24,093
Hey.

116
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:25,594
How're you?

117
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:27,054
How've you been?

118
00:06:30,474 --> 00:06:31,517
Good to see you.

119
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:33,227
-Good to see you.
-Good to see you.

120
00:06:35,521 --> 00:06:37,189
It's hard to know what to say.

121
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:38,857
It's kind of embarrassing.

122
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:41,485
When it's been a while,

123
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:43,362
you'd ask questions like,

124
00:06:43,445 --> 00:06:45,864
"Did you get married,
or, "Did you have kids?"

125
00:06:45,948 --> 00:06:48,492
I mean, I do want a boyfriend.

126
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:52,704
This time, I catch myself
looking back a lot.

127
00:06:52,788 --> 00:06:56,750
Do you think it was good that we broke up?

128
00:06:56,834 --> 00:06:58,585
I've been having trouble moving on.

129
00:06:58,669 --> 00:07:00,129
Is that too heavy?

130
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:03,132
I feel like we've talked
through things a lot.

131
00:07:03,215 --> 00:07:05,175
The biggest thing for me…

132
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:08,720
is that I don't feel like I trust you.

133
00:07:08,804 --> 00:07:13,517
I've held back what I really feel,
bottling it all up.

134
00:07:14,143 --> 00:07:16,770
I didn't think I could beat your ex-wife.

135
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:21,775
What kind of person am I?

136
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:24,736
Honestly, I didn't want to see you.

137
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,989
Is he still hung up on the past?

138
00:07:27,072 --> 00:07:30,367
Looks like they still have
some unresolved issues.

139
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:32,828
She mentioned his ex-wife.

140
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,454
Right, she said something like

141
00:07:34,538 --> 00:07:37,791
she was no match for his ex-wife.

142
00:07:37,875 --> 00:07:39,126
I wonder what that story was.

143
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,419
Kaede-san!

144
00:07:40,502 --> 00:07:42,004
It was Kaede-san who said it.

145
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,339
Hiroyoshi seems like he's been married.

146
00:07:44,423 --> 00:07:46,133
You're right.

147
00:07:46,216 --> 00:07:47,259
Just has that vibe.

148
00:07:47,342 --> 00:07:49,386
Daichi-san seems like

149
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:51,847
he's a CEO of a company or something.

150
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:54,099
Could he alone account for
about three of them?

151
00:07:54,183 --> 00:07:57,477
It's possible Daichi-san accounts
for three on his own.

152
00:07:57,561 --> 00:07:59,897
Three blue ones.

153
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,815
It's still just one flower in that case!

154
00:08:01,899 --> 00:08:04,943
Well then,
here's to making great memories.

155
00:08:05,027 --> 00:08:07,279
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

156
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:12,409
"Here is a review of
all the detailed rules for the hocance.

157
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:16,288
Occupations and ages can't be shared
until they're instructed.

158
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:20,667
They are also not allowed
to reveal who their X is.

159
00:08:20,751 --> 00:08:23,086
Also, regarding the house rules,
during their stay,

160
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:25,923
they are all expected to gather
for dinner each night

161
00:08:26,006 --> 00:08:29,051
but are free to do as they please
the rest of the time.

162
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:31,720
People who have jobs
are permitted to go to work.

163
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:36,141
Our stage is a hotel with over 50 floors
located in Yokohama.

164
00:08:36,225 --> 00:08:38,685
The hotel accommodations
are spacious, private rooms

165
00:08:38,769 --> 00:08:41,104
that even come with
their own mini-kitchen.

166
00:08:41,188 --> 00:08:42,689
Additionally, for common areas,

167
00:08:42,773 --> 00:08:44,858
there is the living room
equipped with a main kitchen,

168
00:08:44,942 --> 00:08:47,152
and a lounge that boasts a beautiful view.

169
00:08:47,236 --> 00:08:50,656
The hotel allows you to fully enjoy
your dream hocance getaway.

170
00:08:50,739 --> 00:08:53,784
The lounge in particular
is a famous spot for secret meetings

171
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:56,787
where couples seek privacy
and endless drama unfolds."

172
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:59,748
A "secret meeting" in the lounge
packs a real punch.

173
00:09:01,083 --> 00:09:02,042
True.

174
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:03,085
That's intense.

175
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:04,336
Totally.

176
00:09:05,921 --> 00:09:07,881
Would you like something to drink?

177
00:09:09,925 --> 00:09:12,094
What's that over there?

178
00:09:12,594 --> 00:09:13,887
What's that red drink?

179
00:09:13,971 --> 00:09:16,473
I'm guessing it's like a lemon
or a strawberry type drink.

180
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:18,433
-Lemon sounds good.
-Yeah?

181
00:09:18,517 --> 00:09:19,977
-Is that okay?
-Sure.

182
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,645
Thank you. You're so sweet.

183
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:25,857
Satoshi is being considerate.

184
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:27,442
True.

185
00:09:28,277 --> 00:09:29,653
Thank you. Wait, there's lemon in it!

186
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:30,612
He's so kind.

187
00:09:30,696 --> 00:09:31,571
Thank you.

188
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,201
What?

189
00:09:36,994 --> 00:09:38,453
Is it not too sour?

190
00:09:38,537 --> 00:09:39,746
I love sour.

191
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:41,206
What's this now?

192
00:09:45,294 --> 00:09:48,088
Mao-san was so easy to talk to.

193
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:51,341
Plus, I got a very good vibe from her.

194
00:09:51,425 --> 00:09:52,592
I'd say Mao-san.

195
00:09:52,676 --> 00:09:54,219
So many picked Mao-san!

196
00:09:54,303 --> 00:09:56,888
Mao-san looked the prettiest to me.

197
00:09:57,472 --> 00:10:01,226
Probably Mao-san.
I mean, she's cute and pretty too.

198
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:02,269
Mao-san again?

199
00:10:02,352 --> 00:10:04,187
She's so popular.

200
00:10:04,271 --> 00:10:06,023
Is this fine here?

201
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,274
Thank you.

202
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:09,609
Do you have any allergies, Mao-san?

203
00:10:09,693 --> 00:10:13,363
I can't have caffeine.

204
00:10:13,447 --> 00:10:15,782
I'm not sure if it's an allergy,

205
00:10:15,866 --> 00:10:17,826
but I get a headache when I have caffeine.

206
00:10:17,909 --> 00:10:19,661
I'm the same.

207
00:10:20,454 --> 00:10:23,290
I can handle something
like matcha or chocolate.

208
00:10:23,373 --> 00:10:25,625
He just forced a connection between them.

209
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:30,756
Standard caffeinated drinks
are a little rough on me.

210
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:36,178
We got a notification.

211
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:37,929
We got a message.

212
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:39,514
Indeed.

213
00:10:40,432 --> 00:10:44,019
"Please open the wooden box under
the flowers in the center of the table."

214
00:10:45,729 --> 00:10:46,855
Where?

215
00:10:46,938 --> 00:10:48,190
I didn't even notice it.

216
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,859
There are so many letters here.

217
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:52,444
Just read the red one?

218
00:10:52,527 --> 00:10:55,030
Just the red one.

219
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:56,615
That took me by surprise.

220
00:10:58,617 --> 00:11:02,079
"These are the letters of introductions
written by your X.

221
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:05,457
Please take turns reading aloud

222
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,167
the letters with your name on it."

223
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:11,713
Here we go.

224
00:11:13,382 --> 00:11:14,508
Thanks.

225
00:11:22,099 --> 00:11:23,183
I'll read it now.

226
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:24,476
"Dear Mao,

227
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:28,021
I'm probably really nervous right now

228
00:11:28,105 --> 00:11:30,649
because I've never written you
a letter before.

229
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:39,741
Mao often smiles and bursts into laughter

230
00:11:39,825 --> 00:11:41,159
at the most unexpected times.

231
00:11:41,243 --> 00:11:43,870
And also bursts into tears

232
00:11:43,954 --> 00:11:46,581
at the most unexpected moments.

233
00:11:46,665 --> 00:11:48,291
She has a childlike innocence

234
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:51,002
and wears her heart on her sleeve."

235
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,088
Great, I'm crying now.

236
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:56,383
It's perfectly normal to cry here.

237
00:11:57,634 --> 00:12:01,054
"Mao understood my personality
better than anyone else.

238
00:12:01,138 --> 00:12:03,265
She was always by my side,

239
00:12:03,348 --> 00:12:05,851
supporting me no matter the situation.

240
00:12:05,934 --> 00:12:07,394
Thank you so much.

241
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:09,938
Mao always pushes herself so hard,

242
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:13,733
that people tend to think
she is emotionally tough.

243
00:12:13,817 --> 00:12:16,069
But she would often think of others,

244
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:18,530
taking on their worries
as if they were her own.

245
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:23,034
I actually think she shows her
vulnerability more than most.

246
00:12:23,118 --> 00:12:25,787
To the people we meet on this hocance,

247
00:12:25,871 --> 00:12:27,581
to the men and the women,

248
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:30,459
please take good care of Mao
over the next month."

249
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:32,043
That is all.

250
00:12:33,962 --> 00:12:35,255
I'm crying.

251
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:38,967
I'm crying just like the letter said.

252
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,261
That's impressive.

253
00:12:41,344 --> 00:12:42,762
Thank you very much.

254
00:12:43,889 --> 00:12:45,265
Well…

255
00:12:47,434 --> 00:12:51,897
they were happy tears, as I realized
how much he really understood me.

256
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:57,110
There's also a feeling of anger

257
00:12:57,569 --> 00:12:58,778
that this is all coming too late.

258
00:12:58,862 --> 00:12:59,738
Right.

259
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:04,117
Writing all that in the letter
at this point.

260
00:13:04,201 --> 00:13:06,536
He knows I cry easily,

261
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,456
so I bet he just wrote
what he thinks people want to hear.

262
00:13:09,539 --> 00:13:11,416
I just know it.

263
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,584
So she was also angry.

264
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:16,087
The reason we broke up

265
00:13:16,671 --> 00:13:20,634
is because he did something
he definitely shouldn't have.

266
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:26,139
If part of him realizes that what he did
was really messed up,

267
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:30,769
then that would be
my sweet little revenge.

268
00:13:31,645 --> 00:13:32,812
Revenge?

269
00:13:32,896 --> 00:13:34,606
-Revenge!
-Seriously?

270
00:13:46,451 --> 00:13:47,577
You look nervous.

271
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:52,040
Who could it be?

272
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:57,671
If you mix truth with lies,

273
00:13:57,754 --> 00:14:00,215
I end up believing you.

274
00:14:00,298 --> 00:14:02,634
I'm very sorry for all the trouble
I've caused.

275
00:14:02,717 --> 00:14:04,886
Realizing how easily
you were betraying me,

276
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:07,055
that hits me the hardest.

277
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:08,348
I'm sorry about that.

278
00:14:08,431 --> 00:14:10,100
Everyone's apologizing for something.

279
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:12,352
I figured there was no point
being together.

280
00:14:12,435 --> 00:14:13,520
It wasn't productive.

281
00:14:13,603 --> 00:14:15,522
You make me sound like I'm the worst.

282
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:17,440
Wait, you didn't realize that? I see.

283
00:14:17,524 --> 00:14:19,818
-She's smiling.
-I'm starting to get scared.

284
00:14:19,901 --> 00:14:22,571
You're right. I'm sorry.

285
00:14:22,654 --> 00:14:25,615
Even if we got back together,

286
00:14:25,699 --> 00:14:27,534
we'd just end up right back here.

287
00:14:28,118 --> 00:14:30,036
You're right.

288
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,580
That's certainly true.

289
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:38,670
"So Mao-san was in tears
from the first letter,

290
00:14:38,753 --> 00:14:41,673
but we discovered she is furious
with her X.

291
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:44,551
She mentioned that the reason
for their breakup

292
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:47,429
was over something heinous her X did.

293
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:48,805
Who do you think her X is?"

294
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:53,226
I don't think it's Hikaru
since he mentioned the caffeine thing.

295
00:14:53,310 --> 00:14:54,603
True.

296
00:14:54,686 --> 00:14:57,105
He also picked her as having
the best first impression.

297
00:14:57,188 --> 00:14:59,316
Hiroyoshi also mentioned

298
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:00,859
-his preference for her.
-And Ryo.

299
00:15:00,942 --> 00:15:01,943
So it's not them.

300
00:15:02,027 --> 00:15:04,154
-Ryo also mentioned her.
-Right.

301
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:05,697
So it's either Daichi or Satoshi.

302
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:06,865
Right.

303
00:15:06,948 --> 00:15:08,408
What do you think it is,

304
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:09,951
the heinous thing he did?

305
00:15:10,035 --> 00:15:12,746
Was it a relationship thing?

306
00:15:12,829 --> 00:15:14,873
Or was it a deeper betrayal of trust?

307
00:15:14,956 --> 00:15:16,166
You think it's that bad?

308
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:17,917
Something out of the question.

309
00:15:18,001 --> 00:15:19,419
It has to be.

310
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:22,130
Probably cheating, right?

311
00:15:22,213 --> 00:15:23,214
Or something like that?

312
00:15:23,298 --> 00:15:26,134
-But there are different levels to that.
-Right.

313
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:27,844
Like a line that shouldn't
have been crossed.

314
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:30,513
That's possible, but what could it be?

315
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:33,516
Like he made a move on her friend.

316
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,559
I see…

317
00:15:34,643 --> 00:15:36,311
So, something close to home.

318
00:15:36,394 --> 00:15:38,104
That's something unacceptable.

319
00:15:38,188 --> 00:15:40,190
Don't make moves on friends, okay?

320
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:41,733
What are you warning me for?

321
00:15:41,816 --> 00:15:44,319
-Good night!
-Good night.

322
00:15:44,402 --> 00:15:45,945
See you tomorrow.

323
00:15:52,243 --> 00:15:53,453
Something's arrived.

324
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:54,663
There's a letter.

325
00:16:00,627 --> 00:16:03,797
"This is the card key for the DVD room…"

326
00:16:04,381 --> 00:16:07,217
"In the DVD room, each participant

327
00:16:07,801 --> 00:16:11,096
can watch their interviews conducted
before the hocance.

328
00:16:11,179 --> 00:16:16,393
However, you can only use the room once
during the hocance."

329
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,979
"And you can only watch one DVD."

330
00:16:20,939 --> 00:16:22,857
Whose do you watch and when?

331
00:16:22,941 --> 00:16:24,734
They only get one shot.

332
00:16:24,818 --> 00:16:27,821
They can see what their X was thinking
at the time.

333
00:16:27,904 --> 00:16:30,949
Or they can see what the person
they're interested in now was thinking.

334
00:16:31,032 --> 00:16:32,033
I see.

335
00:16:41,876 --> 00:16:42,794
She fell asleep.

336
00:16:43,253 --> 00:16:44,796
She's thinking.

337
00:16:44,879 --> 00:16:46,673
She was thinking, not sleeping.

338
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:50,051
Are there people who watch it right away?

339
00:16:50,135 --> 00:16:51,511
There must be.

340
00:16:52,679 --> 00:16:55,056
I wonder if she watched it.

341
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:57,892
ROKKAKUBASHI SHOPPING AREA

342
00:16:57,976 --> 00:16:59,519
Do you have any salmon?

343
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:00,603
We do.

344
00:17:01,646 --> 00:17:02,605
Do you want salmon?

345
00:17:02,689 --> 00:17:03,773
By the block?

346
00:17:04,441 --> 00:17:05,900
They have chocolate ones, too.

347
00:17:05,984 --> 00:17:07,861
They look good.

348
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:10,363
Can I get white chocolate?
It says it's a winter limited edition.

349
00:17:10,447 --> 00:17:11,281
Sure.

350
00:17:14,826 --> 00:17:16,035
Mao-san, can you taste this?

351
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:18,997
You can use the spoon.

352
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,039
I'll get lipstick on it.

353
00:17:20,123 --> 00:17:21,207
Hold on.

354
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:23,752
He called her Mao-san.

355
00:17:25,253 --> 00:17:26,796
Is it good?

356
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:28,548
Everyone's on edge.

357
00:17:28,631 --> 00:17:29,924
Because they're all gunning for her.

358
00:17:30,008 --> 00:17:31,092
They all want Mao-san.

359
00:17:31,176 --> 00:17:33,261
Everyone has mixed feelings.

360
00:17:33,928 --> 00:17:35,680
What are we supposed to do here?

361
00:17:35,764 --> 00:17:38,057
What can we do from the sidelines here?

362
00:17:38,141 --> 00:17:39,142
Just watch.

363
00:17:39,225 --> 00:17:40,769
Is it okay just to watch?

364
00:17:40,852 --> 00:17:43,396
With some feeling of reluctance,
of course.

365
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,773
That's totally fine.

366
00:17:44,856 --> 00:17:46,900
They're going to cook it all themselves.

367
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,401
To earn brownie points?

368
00:17:48,485 --> 00:17:49,486
That's unexpected.

369
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:50,653
Don't worry about it.

370
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:53,615
Looking good!

371
00:17:53,698 --> 00:17:54,657
How does it smell?

372
00:17:55,325 --> 00:17:59,871
I'm on picture duty, then.

373
00:17:59,954 --> 00:18:01,080
How's it looking?

374
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:02,749
Looking nice.

375
00:18:05,293 --> 00:18:06,461
Very nice.

376
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:09,214
Great, that's some nice balance.

377
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:11,508
This is really good.

378
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,301
Hikaru seems bothered by it.

379
00:18:13,384 --> 00:18:14,344
You're right.

380
00:18:15,637 --> 00:18:18,097
-Now we put it in the oven.
-Great idea!

381
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,850
You know, after we bake it…

382
00:18:20,934 --> 00:18:22,393
This is going to be awesome.

383
00:18:25,688 --> 00:18:27,065
He went back to his room.

384
00:18:27,148 --> 00:18:29,859
He went back, for real?

385
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:31,236
Maybe he went to get something.

386
00:18:31,319 --> 00:18:32,153
Yeah.

387
00:18:44,624 --> 00:18:48,127
I want to change into something
more comfortable.

388
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:49,337
That's a good idea.

389
00:18:56,636 --> 00:18:58,179
Is he going to follow him? Never mind.

390
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:01,015
He went in.

391
00:19:08,064 --> 00:19:09,691
-Already?
-Wow, so quick.

392
00:19:21,077 --> 00:19:23,496
"Do not share any information obtained
from this footage

393
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:26,749
with anyone other
than the person involved."

394
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:33,256
So he picked Mao-san after all.

395
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,632
He was curious about her.

396
00:19:39,637 --> 00:19:40,513
Yes, I have.

397
00:19:40,597 --> 00:19:42,181
She has.

398
00:19:42,265 --> 00:19:43,683
So Mao-san was married before.

399
00:19:45,226 --> 00:19:47,228
I have two children.

400
00:19:47,937 --> 00:19:49,272
My eldest is 15.

401
00:19:50,106 --> 00:19:51,441
My youngest is 13.

402
00:19:56,029 --> 00:19:57,780
Let's see…

403
00:19:58,364 --> 00:20:00,742
I'd say I'm leaning 85% towards new love.

404
00:20:06,956 --> 00:20:10,418
What I'm looking for in a new partner
is sincerity.

405
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:14,088
Someone I feel comfortable around.

406
00:20:14,172 --> 00:20:18,009
Someone I can see myself
walking in the same direction with.

407
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:27,268
I'm glad I learned this information.

408
00:20:28,144 --> 00:20:33,149
I'm trying to figure out
how to approach her.

409
00:20:34,359 --> 00:20:37,946
I want to make moves that I won't regret.

410
00:20:40,031 --> 00:20:41,199
It's so creamy.

411
00:20:41,282 --> 00:20:42,659
Can I borrow this cutting board?

412
00:20:45,495 --> 00:20:46,371
Thanks.

413
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:55,838
He's starting to make an effort.

414
00:20:55,922 --> 00:20:57,215
Hikaru's awakened.

415
00:20:57,298 --> 00:20:58,716
He's flipped the switch.

416
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,176
He's a chef!

417
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,094
He must be.

418
00:21:01,177 --> 00:21:02,095
He's a master chef!

419
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:04,597
-Of Japanese cuisine.
-He's a Japanese chef?

420
00:21:05,223 --> 00:21:06,808
Hika-chan, how are you so good?

421
00:21:08,559 --> 00:21:09,519
It's just luck.

422
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:13,481
It's basically pufferfish.

423
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:15,650
-You're really good at it.
-Wow.

424
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,819
-I love to eat.
-You're really good at it.

425
00:21:17,902 --> 00:21:19,195
I like eating.

426
00:21:27,704 --> 00:21:30,164
Did you add honey, Satoshi-san?

427
00:21:30,248 --> 00:21:32,417
Honey and Worcestershire sauce?

428
00:21:33,376 --> 00:21:34,544
That was close.

429
00:21:36,087 --> 00:21:37,463
That was kissing distance.

430
00:21:37,547 --> 00:21:39,465
Yikes.

431
00:21:39,549 --> 00:21:40,758
We nearly had a moment there.

432
00:21:40,842 --> 00:21:41,843
Did you kiss?

433
00:21:44,887 --> 00:21:46,556
Is it Satoshi?

434
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,975
-Satoshi-san?
-I knew it.

435
00:21:49,058 --> 00:21:50,101
That was close!

436
00:21:50,184 --> 00:21:51,686
That was a really close call.

437
00:21:52,562 --> 00:21:54,689
Thank you for this incredible feast!

438
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:57,734
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

439
00:21:58,317 --> 00:22:02,822
Seriously, thank you very much.

440
00:22:02,905 --> 00:22:03,906
It's so good.

441
00:22:03,990 --> 00:22:05,241
So yummy.

442
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:06,909
Wow, that's good.

443
00:22:07,577 --> 00:22:09,996
That's good.

444
00:22:10,079 --> 00:22:13,416
Please help yourselves, there's more.

445
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:15,084
It just dinged.

446
00:22:15,168 --> 00:22:17,628
Go ahead and keep eating,
I'll read it out loud.

447
00:22:21,049 --> 00:22:22,050
Wow!

448
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:23,092
What?

449
00:22:23,176 --> 00:22:27,430
Starting today, we're allowed
to share our occupation?

450
00:22:29,140 --> 00:22:30,266
It's okay?

451
00:22:30,349 --> 00:22:32,685
Let's all point to someone
and guess their occupation.

452
00:22:32,769 --> 00:22:33,686
Okay, great idea.

453
00:22:33,770 --> 00:22:35,104
Ready?

454
00:22:35,772 --> 00:22:37,523
Hiro-san or Hika-chan.

455
00:22:37,607 --> 00:22:38,608
Let's start with Hiro-san.

456
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:39,817
Okay, let's do that.

457
00:22:39,901 --> 00:22:42,195
Okay, so what do you think?

458
00:22:42,278 --> 00:22:44,906
You're a city council member.

459
00:22:44,989 --> 00:22:48,242
Actually, I thought you were
a public servant, too.

460
00:22:48,326 --> 00:22:50,745
It's really nothing special.
Should I give it away?

461
00:22:50,828 --> 00:22:51,996
I'm a dance instructor.

462
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,915
For real?

463
00:22:55,124 --> 00:22:56,793
That was so unexpected.

464
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:01,172
Okay, he wouldn't have had an opportunity
to showcase that.

465
00:23:01,255 --> 00:23:02,090
True.

466
00:23:02,673 --> 00:23:06,469
Do you have anything in mind for Hikaru?

467
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:09,263
I think he's a chef.

468
00:23:09,347 --> 00:23:10,223
Really?

469
00:23:10,306 --> 00:23:12,558
I'm a hardcore chef.

470
00:23:12,642 --> 00:23:14,060
Yeah!

471
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:15,186
-For real?
-Good job.

472
00:23:16,771 --> 00:23:17,897
That makes sense.

473
00:23:17,980 --> 00:23:18,815
A chef?

474
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:20,191
-What kind?
-I'm a French chef.

475
00:23:20,274 --> 00:23:22,527
Wow! Hold on!

476
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:24,195
French?

477
00:23:24,278 --> 00:23:25,738
That's so cool!

478
00:23:25,822 --> 00:23:27,657
That's cool.

479
00:23:28,491 --> 00:23:29,408
Occupation.

480
00:23:29,492 --> 00:23:30,409
Occupation.

481
00:23:30,493 --> 00:23:31,828
Maybe an announcer?

482
00:23:31,911 --> 00:23:34,122
You seriously have a voice made for TV.

483
00:23:34,205 --> 00:23:36,374
Well, I do use my voice.

484
00:23:36,457 --> 00:23:37,708
A voice actress!

485
00:23:37,792 --> 00:23:39,168
I'm an artist.

486
00:23:40,002 --> 00:23:41,129
A musician.

487
00:23:41,212 --> 00:23:43,464
An artist? She's a singer?

488
00:23:43,548 --> 00:23:46,843
So she's a singer. That's cool.

489
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:48,845
-What about you, Kaede?
-What do you think?

490
00:23:48,928 --> 00:23:50,972
-A model.
-Yeah, a model.

491
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:52,557
I think she's like a female CEO.

492
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:53,808
I think so too.

493
00:23:53,891 --> 00:23:55,434
The correct answer is…

494
00:23:56,519 --> 00:23:58,229
I'm a cosmetics brand founder.

495
00:23:58,604 --> 00:24:00,857
-Cosmetics?
-Management!

496
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:04,443
Management for a cosmetics brand,
that sounds nice.

497
00:24:05,403 --> 00:24:06,737
Okay, Yoko-san is next.

498
00:24:06,821 --> 00:24:08,698
I have absolutely no idea!

499
00:24:08,781 --> 00:24:11,242
But I think she's in the beauty industry.

500
00:24:11,325 --> 00:24:12,201
Really?

501
00:24:12,285 --> 00:24:13,661
I think she's an executive assistant.

502
00:24:13,744 --> 00:24:14,829
Yeah.

503
00:24:14,912 --> 00:24:16,289
Like a CEO's secretary.

504
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:19,750
I run a company.

505
00:24:19,834 --> 00:24:21,502
I run a beauty salon

506
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:24,297
I also run a company

507
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:26,966
that develops supplements.

508
00:24:27,049 --> 00:24:28,759
Wow!

509
00:24:30,052 --> 00:24:31,470
What about you, Kana-chan?

510
00:24:31,554 --> 00:24:34,473
I have no idea.

511
00:24:34,557 --> 00:24:36,100
Maybe a nurse?

512
00:24:36,184 --> 00:24:38,186
I'm guessing you're in marketing.

513
00:24:38,269 --> 00:24:42,273
After graduating from university,
I worked in apparel,

514
00:24:42,356 --> 00:24:46,402
then I worked for an airline
for over ten years.

515
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:47,528
She was a flight attendant!

516
00:24:48,738 --> 00:24:51,240
-A flight attendant?
-Is she really?

517
00:24:52,658 --> 00:24:55,953
I think you have a lot of different jobs,
not just one.

518
00:24:56,037 --> 00:24:57,538
I'm guessing hairdresser.

519
00:24:57,622 --> 00:25:00,041
I can see that.

520
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:02,835
The correct answer is…

521
00:25:02,919 --> 00:25:06,339
management of
a membership-based restaurant.

522
00:25:06,422 --> 00:25:08,341
I can see that.

523
00:25:09,550 --> 00:25:11,844
-He definitely has that late-night aura.
-That's true.

524
00:25:11,928 --> 00:25:12,845
You're right.

525
00:25:12,929 --> 00:25:14,138
A complete mystery.

526
00:25:14,222 --> 00:25:15,431
I wonder what you do, Satoshi.

527
00:25:15,514 --> 00:25:16,557
Barista.

528
00:25:16,641 --> 00:25:18,643
I can see that!

529
00:25:18,726 --> 00:25:19,769
Maybe a bartender.

530
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:21,145
A handsome bartender.

531
00:25:21,229 --> 00:25:22,521
I think he's an actor.

532
00:25:22,605 --> 00:25:23,481
True.

533
00:25:23,564 --> 00:25:25,900
-What's the answer?
-Give us the answer!

534
00:25:25,983 --> 00:25:27,235
I work at a retail store.

535
00:25:28,361 --> 00:25:32,907
I mainly work as a sales associate
for a fashion company.

536
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:35,660
I see.

537
00:25:35,743 --> 00:25:36,953
You do have good style.

538
00:25:37,036 --> 00:25:40,498
I think he might be
in some kind of design.

539
00:25:40,581 --> 00:25:42,583
Okay, you're in eyewear!

540
00:25:42,667 --> 00:25:45,753
I thought that too, for real!

541
00:25:45,836 --> 00:25:47,713
Maybe you design glasses?

542
00:25:48,631 --> 00:25:51,634
The answer is…

543
00:25:51,717 --> 00:25:54,178
I currently own a campsite.

544
00:25:54,262 --> 00:25:55,471
Campsite?

545
