815
00:40:21,378 --> 00:40:24,422
She was with X for over 15 years.

816
00:40:24,965 --> 00:40:26,383
Also, we discovered

817
00:40:26,466 --> 00:40:28,969
the reason for their divorce

818
00:40:29,052 --> 00:40:31,096
was X's embezzlement of household funds."

819
00:40:31,179 --> 00:40:33,640
And she mentioned his business.

820
00:40:33,723 --> 00:40:36,643
-That was a big hint.
-That does serve as a hint for X.

821
00:40:36,726 --> 00:40:38,478
When you think about business,

822
00:40:38,562 --> 00:40:40,564
it sounds like either Daichi or Ryo.

823
00:40:41,273 --> 00:40:43,650
She mentioned supplies.

824
00:40:43,733 --> 00:40:44,860
Did she?

825
00:40:44,943 --> 00:40:46,903
Restaurants and campgrounds
both need supplies.

826
00:40:46,987 --> 00:40:47,946
That's true.

827
00:40:48,029 --> 00:40:50,949
Something about Daichi smells fishy.

828
00:40:51,366 --> 00:40:52,909
What do you mean?

829
00:40:53,618 --> 00:40:55,620
He also gave off a late-night vibe, so…

830
00:40:55,704 --> 00:40:58,582
So now I'm imagining him

831
00:40:58,665 --> 00:41:00,292
trying to sell her car.

832
00:41:00,375 --> 00:41:01,626
I can see that.

833
00:41:01,710 --> 00:41:04,588
-Right, I can easily imagine him doing it.
-But we still don't know.

834
00:41:04,671 --> 00:41:08,466
Up until now, we've only had people
looking out for themselves.

835
00:41:08,550 --> 00:41:12,637
But with children in the picture,
there are now four lives involved.

836
00:41:12,721 --> 00:41:15,974
There is a different heaviness to it.

837
00:41:16,057 --> 00:41:19,644
Money becomes a much bigger priority
when kids are involved.

838
00:41:19,728 --> 00:41:20,896
Right?

839
00:41:20,979 --> 00:41:25,275
Plus, that thing with the educational
insurance was pretty messed up.

840
00:41:25,358 --> 00:41:29,571
Now, right after this, we'll finally
find out the identity of Mao's X!

841
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:32,199
Could you stop getting excited
while reading it?

842
00:41:33,408 --> 00:41:37,913
"There is going to be an incident
coming up that will reveal Mao's X."

843
00:41:37,996 --> 00:41:39,956
We're going to find out who Mao's X is.

844
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,666
I want to see who it is!

845
00:41:58,099 --> 00:41:59,809
Did she go to someone's room?

846
00:42:14,157 --> 00:42:16,034
She rang the doorbell!

847
00:42:19,913 --> 00:42:21,289
I'm done now, so let's go.

848
00:42:27,420 --> 00:42:29,881
-Did she ask her X to meet?
-Did she?

849
00:42:29,965 --> 00:42:31,091
Who's coming?

850
00:42:41,726 --> 00:42:44,437
-He's here! I hear footsteps.
-Who is it?

851
00:42:58,201 --> 00:43:00,287
-Hikaru!
-Seriously?

852
00:43:00,370 --> 00:43:02,122
For real?

853
00:43:06,209 --> 00:43:08,712
It has to be because she's so angry!

854
00:43:08,795 --> 00:43:10,839
She's totally pissed off!

855
00:43:23,226 --> 00:43:27,981
My first restaurant was doing well.

856
00:43:28,064 --> 00:43:30,859
But I wanted to make a name for myself,

857
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:34,279
so in an attempt to expand the business,

858
00:43:34,362 --> 00:43:36,156
I decided to open more locations.

859
00:43:36,239 --> 00:43:38,491
That led to a few problems,

860
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:43,580
and the ultimate reason for the divorce

861
00:43:44,706 --> 00:43:47,667
was that I lied and took money
from the tuition fund,

862
00:43:49,127 --> 00:43:50,962
the car, and things like that.

863
00:43:59,929 --> 00:44:01,514
What do you plan on doing now?

864
00:44:02,223 --> 00:44:03,183
About what?

865
00:44:08,271 --> 00:44:09,522
The hocance?

866
00:44:12,942 --> 00:44:14,819
Before even coming here,

867
00:44:16,363 --> 00:44:17,405
you know,

868
00:44:18,198 --> 00:44:21,868
if there were men here
interested in finding new love,

869
00:44:21,951 --> 00:44:25,080
I figured they'd be drawn to you.

870
00:44:25,163 --> 00:44:28,875
Which is why I went and watched
your DVD at an early stage.

871
00:44:28,958 --> 00:44:30,126
When I did,

872
00:44:31,127 --> 00:44:33,838
I saw on the DVD

873
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:40,470
that you're leaning 85%
towards finding new love.

874
00:44:47,769 --> 00:44:51,106
I mean, 15% is pretty low.

875
00:44:52,690 --> 00:44:53,942
I figure it'll be tough.

876
00:44:54,025 --> 00:44:59,155
I'm not sure what my next move should be.

877
00:44:59,239 --> 00:45:04,244
I'm trying to figure out
how to approach her.

878
00:45:05,286 --> 00:45:08,998
I want to make moves that I won't regret.

879
00:45:16,589 --> 00:45:21,845
I also want to hear your intentions.

880
00:45:23,805 --> 00:45:25,223
It's the opposite, though.

881
00:45:25,306 --> 00:45:26,307
What do you mean?

882
00:45:28,143 --> 00:45:29,269
Isn't it the opposite?

883
00:45:29,978 --> 00:45:30,937
Is it?

884
00:45:31,563 --> 00:45:34,524
You're waiting because you want
to ask me what I want to do?

885
00:45:36,109 --> 00:45:39,737
I told you from the get-go
that I'm never going to change.

886
00:45:39,821 --> 00:45:42,615
But what I did goes way deeper
than a simple apology.

887
00:45:42,699 --> 00:45:44,451
Besides, I've already apologized a ton.

888
00:45:44,534 --> 00:45:46,327
You apologizing

889
00:45:47,704 --> 00:45:49,539
doesn't change anything.

890
00:45:50,665 --> 00:45:53,168
That's why I want to know what you're
planning to do moving forward.

891
00:45:53,835 --> 00:45:55,670
Not about what I want to do.

892
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:56,880
What do you want to do?

893
00:45:56,963 --> 00:45:59,757
I've told you what I want to do
countless times already.

894
00:46:01,384 --> 00:46:02,385
Then tell me again.

895
00:46:04,888 --> 00:46:05,972
Clearly.

896
00:46:07,974 --> 00:46:09,392
That's just hindsight.

897
00:46:09,476 --> 00:46:11,478
I'm not looking for hindsight.

898
00:46:11,561 --> 00:46:14,898
But saying something clearly
would be hindsight.

899
00:46:15,565 --> 00:46:18,067
Then tell me right here
what you want to do.

900
00:46:20,737 --> 00:46:24,782
First, I'm going to
pay you back everything

901
00:46:24,866 --> 00:46:27,410
that I took after lying to you.

902
00:46:27,494 --> 00:46:31,664
And I'm going to do better by our kids.

903
00:46:32,415 --> 00:46:34,751
That includes my living situation.

904
00:46:36,377 --> 00:46:37,337
You want me…

905
00:46:39,172 --> 00:46:40,590
to do better with things like that.

906
00:46:42,133 --> 00:46:43,593
Right? Like for real.

907
00:46:45,386 --> 00:46:47,514
I don't think that's it.

908
00:46:51,601 --> 00:46:54,604
For example, we don't know how long
it will take

909
00:46:56,189 --> 00:46:58,024
until the kids become more independent.

910
00:47:00,109 --> 00:47:02,278
I don't know how long it'll take
to pay back everything.

911
00:47:02,362 --> 00:47:05,823
So, what are you planning to do

912
00:47:06,282 --> 00:47:08,117
during that time?

913
00:47:08,201 --> 00:47:11,204
I understand that you want
to get back to working for yourself.

914
00:47:12,080 --> 00:47:13,289
On your own.

915
00:47:13,373 --> 00:47:16,751
Lately, I haven't even mentioned
wanting to work for myself again.

916
00:47:17,544 --> 00:47:20,088
I haven't done anything for myself
these last two years.

917
00:47:23,341 --> 00:47:25,760
I thought about taking a break
from cooking.

918
00:47:26,261 --> 00:47:29,180
It's only been about a year since I quit.

919
00:47:29,264 --> 00:47:32,559
Right now, I work in demolition
and civil engineering.

920
00:47:32,642 --> 00:47:35,520
I oversee roadwork and such.

921
00:47:35,603 --> 00:47:38,898
Currently, I'm not carrying…

922
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:41,985
that much debt.

923
00:47:49,617 --> 00:47:50,493
The thing is,

924
00:47:52,453 --> 00:47:54,914
that's how things were.

925
00:47:54,998 --> 00:47:57,250
But now you've quit your demolition job.

926
00:47:57,333 --> 00:48:00,253
So what are you going to do next?

927
00:48:00,336 --> 00:48:02,589
I want to hear what you're thinking.

928
00:48:03,381 --> 00:48:05,758
I'll work and cook.

929
00:48:06,467 --> 00:48:08,261
I've made that decision.

930
00:48:08,344 --> 00:48:10,346
That's what I'm asking you to tell me!

931
00:48:12,056 --> 00:48:14,267
Why don't you share those important things
with me?

932
00:48:19,022 --> 00:48:20,940
Why won't you tell me that?

933
00:48:23,109 --> 00:48:27,030
Like whether or not you'll face what
you did to us and make amends.

934
00:48:27,113 --> 00:48:29,782
I've never not faced what I've done.

935
00:48:29,866 --> 00:48:31,117
Why can you only say it that way?

936
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:33,286
Because it's true.

937
00:48:34,162 --> 00:48:37,957
If someone were to ask me
what motivates me,

938
00:48:40,251 --> 00:48:41,836
it's obviously you

939
00:48:41,919 --> 00:48:43,713
and the kids.

940
00:48:44,589 --> 00:48:45,798
I mean, yeah, but…

941
00:48:48,051 --> 00:48:50,511
I think I'm 100% at fault.

942
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:54,057
But you tell me that love isn't enough.

943
00:48:54,682 --> 00:48:58,936
You can't see my sincerity,
only that I betrayed you.

944
00:48:59,020 --> 00:49:01,981
You said that it was impossible
for you to move past it.

945
00:49:03,191 --> 00:49:05,568
So you're considering finding new love.

946
00:49:06,653 --> 00:49:10,073
I'm here participating in this because
you asked me to face what I've done.

947
00:49:14,535 --> 00:49:16,829
So what's wrong with me trying to respect
what you want to do.

948
00:49:18,164 --> 00:49:22,293
After all the things I've done,

949
00:49:22,377 --> 00:49:25,963
there's a chance that I never
truly considered you

950
00:49:28,424 --> 00:49:30,593
or your feelings.

951
00:49:30,677 --> 00:49:31,511
You haven't.

952
00:49:31,594 --> 00:49:33,262
That might be the case.

953
00:49:33,930 --> 00:49:37,183
So all I can tell you during this hocance,

954
00:49:39,268 --> 00:49:41,604
is that I still love you.

955
00:49:42,355 --> 00:49:45,775
And if you tell me that's not enough
and it's meaningless,

956
00:49:46,776 --> 00:49:50,822
then all I can do is help you
find new love.

957
00:49:54,242 --> 00:49:56,577
I'm even fine with leaving the show
right now.

958
00:49:56,661 --> 00:49:58,037
That's how I feel.

959
00:50:00,123 --> 00:50:01,958
To me, it doesn't matter.

960
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:04,085
This hocance.

961
00:50:06,838 --> 00:50:10,258
Why do you say it that way?

962
00:50:10,341 --> 00:50:11,718
What do you mean?

963
00:50:11,801 --> 00:50:12,969
You haven't changed at all.

964
00:50:14,429 --> 00:50:16,347
Even though you're at fault,

965
00:50:17,640 --> 00:50:21,936
it doesn't resonate because you don't make
it sound like you're at fault.

966
00:50:22,562 --> 00:50:24,063
What do you mean, I say it all the time.

967
00:50:24,147 --> 00:50:27,817
The way you say, "What do you mean"
makes me feel like you don't believe it.

968
00:50:35,783 --> 00:50:37,326
So really,

969
00:50:37,410 --> 00:50:41,497
it makes me feel like
you're not actually prioritizing

970
00:50:43,332 --> 00:50:45,585
the people you say are important to you.

971
00:50:53,676 --> 00:50:56,512
The reason I worked so hard
to save up that money

972
00:50:56,596 --> 00:51:00,224
was because I wanted to take a trip
around the world with you in the future.

973
00:51:06,606 --> 00:51:08,399
I wanted to see the aurora.

974
00:51:18,785 --> 00:51:19,911
You know.

975
00:51:24,540 --> 00:51:28,669
There were things
I kept secret from you, too.

976
00:51:29,504 --> 00:51:31,088
But those were all things

977
00:51:32,840 --> 00:51:35,343
I ultimately did with you in mind.

978
00:52:12,588 --> 00:52:16,634
We got married exactly one year later

979
00:52:16,717 --> 00:52:18,761
because I got pregnant.

980
00:52:18,845 --> 00:52:23,975
That pushed us to get married.

981
00:52:35,570 --> 00:52:40,199
I remember you said you wanted your own
restaurant on Kokusaidori by 30.

982
00:52:40,283 --> 00:52:43,119
And you actually accomplished that
by age 31 or 32.

983
00:52:43,202 --> 00:52:46,497
At the time, I was genuinely impressed.

984
00:52:56,507 --> 00:52:58,342
Wow, that's amazing!

985
00:52:58,426 --> 00:52:59,927
So I guess he was a go-getter.

986
00:53:00,011 --> 00:53:01,929
I see.

987
00:53:19,155 --> 00:53:21,115
He'd come home when we were all asleep,

988
00:53:21,198 --> 00:53:24,368
so I was in charge of household chores
and taking care of the kids.

989
00:53:24,452 --> 00:53:28,789
And when he stopped making money,
everything was on me.

990
00:53:30,041 --> 00:53:33,878
Use the products to create
contrast between light and dark tones.

991
00:53:33,961 --> 00:53:37,465
I worked whenever I had any spare time
to help support my family.

992
00:53:37,548 --> 00:53:40,593
I pushed hard raising them that way.

993
00:53:50,519 --> 00:53:55,107
At that point, I wanted to cut ties
with him completely.

994
00:53:55,191 --> 00:53:59,236
When it came to the divorce,
we were already separated.

995
00:53:59,320 --> 00:54:02,740
I just sent him the divorce papers,
and we barely even talked.

996
00:54:02,823 --> 00:54:06,369
I just decided on my own
that I couldn't handle it anymore.

997
00:54:06,452 --> 00:54:09,121
Ready, set, let's eat.

998
00:54:10,039 --> 00:54:14,627
I think I was able to push through
because of the kids.

999
00:54:14,710 --> 00:54:18,089
It's all thanks to those two.

1000
00:54:21,676 --> 00:54:25,429
Whenever I think about how I wished
I'd taken them on more trips…

1001
00:54:29,934 --> 00:54:33,980
or given them a happier life,

1002
00:54:34,063 --> 00:54:38,901
it brings me to tears, just like this.

1003
00:55:02,508 --> 00:55:07,096
Maybe we are happier apart,

1004
00:55:07,179 --> 00:55:13,227
but I wanted him to reflect
on what's most important to him.

1005
00:55:13,310 --> 00:55:17,356
And if that's really us, then I'd probably

1006
00:55:18,232 --> 00:55:20,526
reconsider things between us.

1007
00:55:21,569 --> 00:55:27,199
Ultimately, I think it comes down
to where his head is at.

1008
00:55:31,203 --> 00:55:34,040
It's definitely about how you convey it.
